2. DESIGN INVESTIGATION — WHY STRICT WELDED-EDGE ADJACENCY IS NOT ENOUGH
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
The plan says to build face adjacency from the welded triangle soup f_arr.
Diagnostic on the seam fixture (test_seam_duplicated_touching_quads_merge):

  offset = 1.5e-4; extent = 4.0; quant_step = 0.0 (single-occurrence delta
  ignored by the recurrence guard); eps = max(1e-9, 1e-7*extent) = 4e-7.
  Welded tris: [(0,1,2),(0,2,3),(4,5,6),(4,6,7)] — quad1 = verts {0,1,2,3},
  quad2 = verts {4,5,6,7}. NO shared edge: the 1.5e-4 seam gap is NOT bridged
  by welding (4e-7 << 1.5e-4) and is NOT bridged by the quant-derived eps
  (quant_step=0 there).

  The separated fixture welds to the SAME shape. So welded f_arr alone cannot
  distinguish the seam case (MUST merge, test asserts 1 face) from the
  genuinely-separated case (MUST NOT merge, tests assert 2 faces). A strict
  welded-edge map would split the seam tests => BUG (previously-merged
  touching case now splits).

  RESOLUTION: cluster vertices within edge_adj_tol = max(1e-5, 5e-4*extent)
  — the extent-based floor of snap_tol, i.e. the exact criterion under which
  _snap_group_vertices would merge the seam vertices anyway. Two edges whose
  endpoints are nearer than that are the same seam edge. Verifies against the
  whole fixture family:
    1.5e-4 seam   <= 2e-3  (extent 4)   -> merged
    2e-4  seam   <= 1.5e-3 (extent 3)   -> merged
    1.5e-4 seam   <= 3e-3  (extent 6)   -> merged
    2.0   gap    >> 2e-3  (extent 4)   -> NOT merged
    vertex-only touch: no edge pair within tol -> NOT merged

3. IMPLEMENTATION
-----------------
mcp_server/mesh_analysis.py (line numbers post-edit):

  _coplanar_with_region(face_plane, region_plane, cos_tol, offset_tol)  L958
    The isolated coplanarity predicate (same cos_tol + offset_tol as the
    global first-match path). T12/R-7 swap point for the running plane-fit.

  _cluster_near_vertices(v_arr, tol)                                     L974
    Deterministic grid-based union-find vertex clustering: each vertex
    probes the 27 cells around its round(coord/tol) key, unions with earlier
    vertices within tol. Returns {vertex_index: cluster_id}.

  _group_planar_triangles(v_arr, f_arr, tri_normals, angle_tol_deg, extent) L1032
    Structure:
      a) Per-face canonical (normal, offset) plane + area, in index order;
         degenerate faces -> None plane (skipped exactly as before).
      b) O(F) edge -> face-list map over the welded soup keyed by CLUSTERED
         vertex ids; symmetric adjacency sets per face.
      c) CONNECTIVITY FIRST PASS (primary): seeds = all valid faces sorted by
         (-area, ti); for each unassigned seed, BFS region-growing over
         sorted(adj[cur]) neighbors that pass _coplanar_with_region against
         the SEED's plane. Deterministic: largest-area seed (smallest index
         on tie), sorted neighbor traversal, region tri_indices sorted.
      d) GLOBAL FALLBACK (unchanged first-match path): remaining unassigned
         faces matched only against fallback-created groups (never against
         connectivity groups — that would re-merge separated coplanar
         patches and defeat R-2). Predicate, group dict shape and skip of
         degenerate faces are byte-identical to the pre-change code.
    Group dict shape unchanged: {"normal", "offset", "tri_indices"}.

  Function signature unchanged. No new dependencies (numpy + stdlib only).

