7. BEHAVIOR CHANGES vs BASELINE
------------------------------
  * Group STRUCTURE for coplanar-but-disconnected patches changed from ONE
    group (global first-match, 2 loops -> 2 faces) to TWO groups (1 loop
    each -> 2 faces). Face-level output (count, area, vertex count, holes)
    is identical for every existing test — the R-2 purpose is to prevent the
    group-level over-merge that the boundary-loop phase then has to untangle.
  * Verified no previously-merged touching case now splits: touching,
    edge-connected-strips, frame-with-hole, seam (1.5e-4 / 2e-4), stacked
    strips, cube, box and quantized-fan fixtures all still merge exactly as
    before (one face, correct area).

